{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Mirror inventory finding F9 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), LOW.\n\n## Problem\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py:326` `LAYER_ORDER = (\"default\", \"user\", \"project\", \"env\", \"cli\")` — canonical\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py:51` `_SOURCE_KINDS` — the same 5, hand-copied\n\n`_operation_config.py:128` validates a provenance label against the copy, and `config.py:337`\ndocuments that domain as \"``label`` ∈ :data:`LAYER_ORDER`\" — so the copy is asserting membership of\nthe canonical tuple while restating it.\n\n## Approach — generate-from-canonical\n\n`_SOURCE_KINDS = frozenset(config.LAYER_ORDER)`.\n\nORDER is the tuple's only additional fact, and the consumer uses the copy purely as a membership\nset (`label not in _SOURCE_KINDS`), so deriving a frozenset from it loses nothing. That is the\ncheck worth stating: a set derivation would be wrong if any consumer depended on precedence, and\nnone does.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `_SOURCE_KINDS` is derived from `config.LAYER_ORDER`, not re-listed. Verified by a test\n      asserting equality with `frozenset(config.LAYER_ORDER)` and the literal being gone.\n- [ ] AC2: a layer added to `LAYER_ORDER` is accepted as a provenance label with no second edit.\n      Verified by a test that extends the compared tuple and asserts the derived set follows.\n- [ ] AC3: no consumer of `_SOURCE_KINDS` relies on ordering, so the tuple -> frozenset conversion\n      is safe. Verified by a test asserting every use site treats it as a membership set.\n- [ ] AC4: an unknown provenance label is still rejected. Verified by an explicit rejection test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"operation_config or config_layer or provenance\" -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788385010714245001,"uuid":"a2e981d7-0822-4464-be24-6421c0833bfb"}